Fat saturation index describes the relative contribution of the saturated fat to the total lipid signal64. The fat saturation index was calculated using MR spectroscopy data. The sum of the terminal methyl protons (–CH3) at 0.9 ppm, the bulk methylene protons (–(CH2)n–) at 1.3 ppm, and the methylene protons (–CH = CHCH2–) at 1.6 ppm represented the saturated fat. The sum of the lipid peak areas of the olefinic protons at 5.3 ppm and 5.4 ppm represented the unsaturated fat. The fat saturation index was calculated as follows:4\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
