We also measured the frequency difference between the bulk methylene protons at 1.3 ppm and the water peak at 4.7 ppm. A decreased frequency difference between the two resonances can indicate a lower iron content66. Iron is a compound with paramagnetic effects and has the potential to change the frequency difference by introducing susceptibility effects and magnetic field inhomogeneities66.

